## Choices

The exercise is test preparation. It appoints no role and adds no module. The proposed packet is eleven commit blobs at the frozen HEAD, 70451 bytes, with one ref slot and 60621 bytes left. The twelfth ref is Claude's real-reader brief. That brief is not sealed. Member `0145.real-reader-brief-0514` held only `01.md` and `reservation.json` at this check. Its bytes are pending. They are not filled from the live lab, and they are not cut to fit.

The dependency is described from released pack `0507.prime-support/evidence/pack05.14/source-manifest.json` and from the pack05.17 pin of `0507.prime-support/05.14.md`. The live page `40c96b9f77118ecfb0a75d1151331a7833b976acd619b521c54441ad4d89a6a1`, 8688 bytes, differs from the commit blob `dd3b9bade334b403f9b5f947c25c689690d317a4956894b6482837505953a290`, 7645 bytes. The live page records a claim and `Execution: IN PROGRESS`, and its review is still `PENDING`. Those live sentences are not committed bytes. Claude's active brief outputs were not opened.

The canonical assignment `0401.goal/06.01.md` names `current_work` `0504.app-entry/05.06.md`. Prime review `0507/evidence/prime-review05.10/review.md` leaves that conflict open. This plan does not elect a lane and does not rewrite the assignment.

The model-facing page is `HOMEWORK.md`. `EVALUATOR.md` stays out of the boot reading order. Expected answers that need the unsealed brief stay unbound.

## Disposition

The packet budget, the accepted pins, and the blocked gaps are in `evidence/cold-prime05.17/`. No unchanged runtime suite was rerun. No orientation attempt was started.

When Prime accepts `0145`, measure that sealed brief against the remaining 60621 bytes and the one open ref. If it fits, add it whole. If it does not fit, record an omission and keep the text uncut. Only after that measurement may the Director run one prepare into an external records directory. This note does not contain a receipt.
